<title>USA: U.S. June business inventories rose 0.7 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. June business inventories rose 0.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. June business inventories rose 0.7 percent after rising 0.2 percent in May. It said June business sales also rose 0.7 percent after a 0.5 percent drop in May.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:    June	May------(Prev)    June'96</p>
<p> Total Business  1,025.94  1,019.03  1,019.33    992.10</p>
<p> Durable Goods     616.83    611.56    611.93    590.64</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  409.11    407.47    407.39    401.46</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:    June	May------(Prev)    June'96</p>
<p> Manufacturers     444.80   443.46     443.32    429.80</p>
<p> Retailers	   317.22   316.54     317.33    306.18</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     87.71    87.61	87.91     85.15</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 263.93   259.03     258.68    256.12</p>
<p>    SALES:	    June	May------(Prev)    June'96</p>
<p> Total Business    747.86   742.95     743.20    712.73</p>
<p> Durable Goods     374.41   368.71     368.90    353.01</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  373.45   374.24     374.31    359.71</p>
<p>    SALES:	    June	May------(Prev)    June'96</p>
<p> Manufacturers     326.43   323.57     323.54    310.05</p>
<p> Retailers	   210.74   209.37     209.31    202.70</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     50.64    49.93	49.85     48.67</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 210.69   210.01     210.35    199.98</p>
<p> Inventory-To-	 June     May------(Prev)    June'96</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.37    1.37	  1.37	1.39</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected June business inventories to rise 0.6 percent.</p>
<p>The department said the 0.7 percent increase in June business inventories was the largest since a 0.8 percent rise in April 1995.</p>
<p>The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
